WEBVTT

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:11.590
This is the focus in question,
Your Majesty.

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:15.180
It's enchanted with increased magical
defense, increased physical defense,

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:19.350
and resists all status ailments,

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.100
and it was created by none
other than Sei Takanashi.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:25.480
An item of legendary power.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:30.150
I understand now why you
insisted we speak in private.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:33.360
You were able to
estimate her abilities, then?

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.780
Yes, Your Majesty.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:38.530
By instructing her to attempt
varying levels of enchantment,

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:40.450
I came to an approximation.

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:44.790
Her ability in Holy-affinity magic is
matched only by the Grand Magus himself,

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:47.460
though she may be even
more powerful than that.

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:57.300
Less than a year since her Summoning,
and already she has such power?

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.810
The logical conclusion, then,
is that she is the Saint, yes?

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:06.900
That is still yet to be determined.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:11.860
Unfortunately, the only mage in the
kingdom with the ability to Appraise her

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:14.490
is the Grand Magus.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:17.410
We will only know whether
this Sei Takanashi is the Saint...

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:20.530
...when he awakens from his deep slumber.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:05.850
Morning!

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:13.150
Oh, Jude! Good morning.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:18.440
I could've helped you
water if you'd asked.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:21.660
Thanks for offering, but I can handle it.

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:29.200
Oh, right! We're going to deliver
potions to the Third Order today.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.370
That's right.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:33.500
Apparently, it's a bigger
delivery than usual,

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:39.170
so the Director wants everyone
who's free to lend a hand.

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:40.880
Are there that many of us who're free?

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:49.350
I swear, Sei...

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:52.060
I <i>told </i>you not to make this many potions!

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:54.520
I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:00.860
Got it. I'll come help deliver potions.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:01.740
You sure?

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:03.160
Yeah, it's no biggie.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:06.240
Besides, I'll get to spend some
time with my new friend!

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:07.490
Wait, who?

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:13.170
There you go! Good job.
You're such a good boy.

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:15.290
Is that you, Sei?

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:16.840
Oh, Ser Wolff!

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:19.250
You come by to deliver potions?

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:21.720
That's right.
I'm glad we can be of service.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:30.020
The potions from the Institute
are something else.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:33.270
They're of a much higher quality
than the ones you find in the market.

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:35.020
How do you guys do it?

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:38.110
I'm afraid that's a trade secret.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:43.240
Heck, <i>I'd </i>like to know why I'm cursed
to make everything 1.5 times stronger.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:47.030
Must be tough on you guys
to craft so many of them for us.

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:48.950
And we're gonna need
even more next time, too.

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.370
Huh?! Even more than this?!

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:53.500
What, you haven't heard?

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:54.500
Heard what?

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:56.670
A month from now,

00:04:56.670 --> 00:05:00.630
we and the Second Order are
going out on a joint expedition.

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:02.800
The extra numbers
are just for safety's sake,

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:05.590
since we'll be heading
into the Ghoshe Forest.

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:09.760
Ghoshe? Oh, that's the forest where
the Salamander attack happened.

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:11.180
The huge delivery makes sense, then.

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:17.060
Oh, the First Order won't be joining you?

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:20.190
Huh?

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:23.440
Am I not supposed to ask about them?

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:28.410
The First Order is helping
out the Crown Prince.

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:29.660
The Crown Prince?

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:35.620
Prince Kyle and his Academy entourage
went to the Eastern Woods to train.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:36.580
Prince Kyle?

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.630
Oh, <i>that guy</i>.

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:44.760
Though I'm not sure how much training
they'll get done over there.

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:46.470
What do you mean?

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:51.640
Like all the areas close to here,
it's relatively peaceful.

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:54.810
So there's nothing to battle there.

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:58.690
I mean, makes sense.
He's got the Saint with him.

00:05:58.690 --> 00:06:00.400
Did you just say the Saint?

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.900
Yeah, she's this girl
in Prince Kyle's care.

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:05.530
We know 'cause he keeps calling her that.

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:07.450
Her name's Aira Misono.

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:17.960
Prince Kyle and his guys are keeping a
close eye on her at the Royal Academy.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:22.290
The Prince is always on about how the
Saint is vital to our kingdom's future,

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:24.590
so he's pulling out all the stops for her.

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:26.050
Makes sense.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.510
I'm glad she's doing okay.

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:35.060
Huh?

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:39.060
You're way more Saintly than
that other Saint girl, Sei.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:43.110
Thank you for the compliment.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:49.280
Everyone likes to joke about it,

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:53.280
but I think I probably <i>am </i>the Saint.

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:58.750
But I don't feel like going out and
announcing that to the world...

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:02.840
Can't I live like a regular person
until someone else figures it out?

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:08.920
Miracle

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:21.520
I can't get that conversation
with the knights out of my head.

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:23.650
I keep thinking about Aira Misono.

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:26.280
From what I've heard about her,

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:30.570
she doesn't have crazy
cheat-code powers like I do.

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:33.240
Why are we on such different levels?

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:36.330
Unfortunately, I think I know the answer.

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:38.700
It's because <i>she's </i>not the Saint at all,

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:41.170
and <i>I'm </i>the <i>real </i>Saint.

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:45.210
But I really don't want that to be true.

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:50.090
My, my, you've sure been
crafting up a storm.

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:51.050
Ser Director!

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:57.180
Sorry. I was lost in thought
and didn't think to stop.

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:58.470
Well, <i>that's </i>nothing new!

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:06.520
And he kicked me out of the lab.

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:13.570
At first, he was worried about my
endless supply of magic power.

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:16.490
Now he's worried about
the Institute's herb supply.

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:27.750
Well, I've got the day off, so I might
as well go do some research!

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:29.000
Let's see...

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:32.970
Maybe I can find a book on herbs to make
potions even better than high-grade!

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:42.940
I've been looking for books
like that for a while now, but...

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:47.480
I'm sure you'd find tomes with that
knowledge in the Forbidden Collection!

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:53.820
Or so Liz said, but I'm guessing normal
people can't just waltz in there.

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:58.450
Holy Affinity Magic

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:01.290
The knights said their next expedition

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:03.910
was into the same forest
as that salamander attack...

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:06.630
Holy

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:10.500
If they come back with
that many casualties again,

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:15.260
could there be some way to help
them outside of just making potions?

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:35.490
Okay. This one's a <i>little </i>too complicated.

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:37.490
Let's find one for beginners.

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:40.410
Do you have an interest
in magic, young lady?

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:43.750
I believe that tome will
be far too difficult for you.

00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:45.500
I was just thinking that.

00:09:45.500 --> 00:09:49.420
I was going to see if I could find
one that covers more basics...

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:54.630
Who <i>is </i>this guy?

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:57.630
Try this one, then.

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:10.690
Hey, this is perfect!
I can totally work with this!

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:12.860
Thank you very much!

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:13.820
Of course.

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:23.580
I've been remiss.
My name is Siegfried Salutania.

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:30.080
Salutania... isn't that
the name of this kingdom?

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:33.590
I believe your name is Sei, is that right?

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:36.550
Y-Yes, pleased to meet you.

00:10:36.550 --> 00:10:42.300
No need for such formality, especially
when I have yet to thank you properly.

00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:49.350
But I haven't done anything for this guy.
Why does he want to thank me?

00:10:49.350 --> 00:10:54.690
I heard my son was quite rude
to you when you arrived.

00:10:54.690 --> 00:10:58.360
Please accept my deepest
apologies for his behavior.

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:00.240
I'm sorry, who?

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:04.990
My first-born son, Kyle.

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:09.290
Kyle... He's the crown prince, right?

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:12.250
So that would make this guy...

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:13.210
The <i>king</i>?!

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:21.550
Oh, gosh, please, rise!

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:25.890
I'm not bothered by that
in the slightest anymore!

00:11:25.890 --> 00:11:31.560
I should have apologized to you
earlier in a more formal capacity.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:35.020
Oh, no! Please, you needn't
worry about that at all!

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:37.110
That's not all I'd hoped
to speak with you about.

00:11:37.110 --> 00:11:41.280
I wish to reward you for the meritorious
deeds you've performed for our kingdom.

00:11:41.280 --> 00:11:43.120
Would you like land,
or perhaps a court title?

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:45.160
No, no, that's all right!

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:47.410
Very well. How about your
own estate in the Capital?

00:11:47.410 --> 00:11:48.580
I couldn't live there by myself!

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:50.290
Then I'll employ some
servants to assist you.

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:51.620
Servants?!

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:55.710
I should have known to trust Johan.

00:11:55.710 --> 00:12:00.590
When I spoke with him about
my intent to reward you properly,

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:05.430
he urged me to reconsider, as you
would likely refuse any offers.

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:06.720
Good job, Johan!

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:15.520
I must go. Forgive me for
interrupting your research.

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:19.400
Mark my words, I <i>will </i>properly
thank you for your service in court.

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:20.650
In <i>court</i>?!

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:44.550
Ow!

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:02.150
Wow.

00:13:02.150 --> 00:13:05.990
It took a while, but I'm so glad
I powered through to learn this!

00:13:05.990 --> 00:13:08.530
Something smells good! What're you up to?

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:12.580
Huh? Oh, you know!
Just making some snacks!

00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:16.830
I heard the Knights are back, but many
are still recovering in the hospital,

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:18.840
so I thought I'd cheer
them up with a little visit.

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:23.800
You know, I think the
Director mentioned that, too.

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:26.340
Okay! I'm gonna head out, then!

00:13:27.930 --> 00:13:29.140
Oh, later.

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:41.480
Hello, everyone!

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:43.900
Hey, it's Sei!

00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:45.360
You came all this way just to visit <i>us</i>?

00:13:47.570 --> 00:13:50.080
How are you all doing?

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:52.240
Right as rain, as you can see!

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:55.540
Please, you were on death's
door when they brought you in!

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:56.580
C'mon, don't tell her!

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:01.590
Sounds like the expedition
was quite the ordeal.

00:14:01.590 --> 00:14:04.720
Yeah, there were hordes
of beasts out there.

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:08.800
But we only made it back 'cause of
those potions you guys made us!

00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:10.180
No doubt about that.

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:11.140
Thank you.

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:15.770
I'm glad we could help.

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:19.310
Man, though, have you ever seen
that many monsters at one time?

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:43.170
Hello!

00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:47.050
Hey, here to visit?

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:52.010
Y-Your arm...

00:14:52.010 --> 00:14:54.720
Yeah, got a little clumsy out there.

00:14:59.980 --> 00:15:02.730
Your potions helped us get back alive,

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:05.900
but they can't do much about this.

00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:11.570
If potions can't help,
what about healing magic?

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:16.450
I dunno. I've had some wounds
healed with magic before.

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:20.870
But this, well...
it's no ordinary flesh wound.

00:15:20.870 --> 00:15:24.710
I'd have to find a high-level mage
who can use holy magic,

00:15:24.710 --> 00:15:27.130
and believe me, that's not gonna be easy.

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:30.380
I'm so sorry.

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:34.680
Thanks for coming to see me.
Glad we could talk one last time.

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:37.140
Huh? What do you mean?

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:39.730
I'm quitting the Order
and heading back home.

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:43.440
Not like I can keep being
a knight with this and all.

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:50.490
I'm a commoner who rose up through
the Academy to become a knight.

00:15:50.490 --> 00:15:56.620
Now that I'm not a knight anymore, I'm
not allowed to stay here at the palace.

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:59.160
I wish I could.

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:03.170
I could do more for this kingdom,
for its people...

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:06.000
But now...

00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:12.300
Wolff...

00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:19.890
If you could have your arm back,
would you want it?

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:34.820
If I heal him here, I won't be able to
pretend I'm an ordinary person anymore.

00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:42.660
If he were just a stranger...

00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:50.340
No, even if he <i>were </i>just a stranger,
I wouldn't be able to walk away.

00:16:50.340 --> 00:16:52.380
I'd stay and help however I could.

00:16:54.890 --> 00:16:58.010
Please, let this heal him!

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:00.560
Heal.

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:27.580
Sei...

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:36.550
Thank you.

00:17:38.470 --> 00:17:40.720
Um...

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:42.720
You're welcome?

00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:49.570
Why are you saying it like a question?

00:17:49.570 --> 00:17:52.610
I-I don't know.

00:17:52.610 --> 00:17:53.740
Oh, c'mon!

00:17:57.240 --> 00:17:58.820
Look!

00:17:58.820 --> 00:18:00.410
What in the world...

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:05.160
That's right.

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:13.300
The other men in this room
are also gravely injured.

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:17.130
When they're done healing, most won't
be able to return to the Order as knights.

00:18:22.890 --> 00:18:23.490
Sei?

00:18:23.490 --> 00:18:24.810
There's no turning back now.

00:18:29.770 --> 00:18:32.320
I'm going to Heal everyone in this room!

00:18:37.860 --> 00:18:39.780
She's incredible!

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:41.280
You have to see this!

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:53.460
I can see... I can see again!

00:18:53.460 --> 00:18:54.510
I can't believe it!

00:18:54.510 --> 00:18:55.630
It's a miracle!

00:18:58.220 --> 00:19:00.970
Sei, you all right?

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:05.350
I'm fine. How many more rooms are left?

00:19:05.350 --> 00:19:06.930
This is the last one.

00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:09.650
We've already gone by the rooms
with the worst injuries,

00:19:09.650 --> 00:19:12.940
so everyone here's only
got cuts and bruises.

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:13.900
Okay.

00:19:21.990 --> 00:19:26.290
There was a high-level
holy magic spell in that book.

00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:33.000
It wouldn't hurt to try it if it's
going to help everyone, right?

00:19:34.420 --> 00:19:39.220
I just have to focus my magic throughout
my whole body, not just my hand...

00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:42.050
Then imagine it filling the whole room...

00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:44.760
Area heal!

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:07.450
Wow. I feel like that drained
all my power out of me...

00:20:07.450 --> 00:20:08.620
I'm healed!

00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:10.910
Same here! My wounds are gone!

00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:15.630
Did you just use an
area-wide healing spell?

00:20:17.380 --> 00:20:19.760
Ser Director! Commander Hawke!

00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:25.550
You sure know how to show off.

00:20:25.550 --> 00:20:30.060
Y-Yeah, I know, I probably
went a little too far...

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:32.940
But I couldn't leave
without doing something.

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:35.190
I have to live up to
everyone's expectations.

00:20:42.950 --> 00:20:44.030
I'm sorry.

00:20:49.790 --> 00:20:52.000
Don't be. You've done well.

00:22:34.980 --> 00:22:36.460
Look, over there.

00:22:36.460 --> 00:22:37.020
What is it?

00:22:37.020 --> 00:22:38.040
That's her, the young woman there.

00:22:38.040 --> 00:22:38.770
I see.

00:22:39.980 --> 00:22:40.900
Lady Sei!

00:22:42.570 --> 00:22:44.280
I've come to escort you home!

00:22:49.450 --> 00:22:50.870
You were escorted home again?

00:22:52.910 --> 00:22:57.830
I tried to tell them no,
but they wouldn't give up, so...

00:22:57.830 --> 00:22:59.790
I suppose you'll have to live with it.

00:22:59.790 --> 00:23:01.080
Ever since that spectacle,

00:23:01.080 --> 00:23:06.050
the Second Order's been whispering
about you being the Saint.

00:23:06.050 --> 00:23:10.050
And they're apparently not the only ones.

00:23:16.390 --> 00:23:21.310
But we'll know if those rumors
hold water soon enough.

00:23:21.310 --> 00:23:25.400
I just received a missive
from the Royal Magi Assembly.

00:23:25.400 --> 00:23:28.900
They're finally ready to have
you and your abilities appraised.

00:23:28.900 --> 00:23:30.410
Sei,

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:34.200
they'd like to Appraise you to
see if you are, indeed, the Saint.

00:23:35.060 --> 00:23:40.060
Next Time

00:23:35.060 --> 00:23:40.060
Appraisal
